# Help: RNBD network block device over RTRS
#
# The RNBD client and server map block devices across an RDMA link
# through the RTRS transport. blktests' rnbd group drives the pair
# over a soft-RoCE link, so rdma_rxe travels along; the group
# refuses the siw default and requires USE_RXE=1.
#
# Prerequisites inlined per the self-containment rule:
# - INFINIBAND=m + INFINIBAND_ADDR_TRANS=y carry the RDMA core and
#   rdma_cm that RTRS rides on.
# - INFINIBAND_RTRS_CLIENT/SERVER=m are the RTRS transport halves
#   the rnbd pair depends on.
#
# Layer builtin/storage/rnbd.config to build the set in (=y) for a
# no-modprobe boot.
# See: drivers/block/rnbd/Kconfig
# See: drivers/infiniband/ulp/rtrs/Kconfig
# See: drivers/infiniband/sw/rxe/Kconfig

#
# Inlined prerequisites
#
CONFIG_INFINIBAND=m
CONFIG_INFINIBAND_ADDR_TRANS=y
CONFIG_INFINIBAND_RTRS_CLIENT=m
CONFIG_INFINIBAND_RTRS_SERVER=m
CONFIG_RDMA_RXE=m

#
# RNBD client and server
#
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RNBD_CLIENT=m
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RNBD_SERVER=m
